  rules: [
    "1️⃣ QACHON ISHLATILADI?\n\nPresent Continuous to'rtta asosiy holatda ishlatiladi:\n\n📌 HOZIR BO'LAYOTGAN HARAKAT (Now): Aynan hozir, shu vaqtda sodir bo'layotgan ishlar.\n  → I am reading a book right now. (Men hozir kitob o'qiyapman)\n  → She is watching TV at the moment. (U hozir televizor ko'ryapti)\n\n📌 VAQTINCHALIK HOLAT (Temporary): Hozirgi paytda davom etayotgan, lekin doimiy bo'lmagan harakatlar.\n  → I am staying with my friend this week. (Men bu hafta do'stimnikida turibman)\n  → He is working on a special project this month. (U bu oy maxsus loyiha ustida ishlayapti)\n\n📌 KELAJAK REJALAR (Future plans): Kelajak uchun aniq rejalashtirilgan, tayinlangan harakatlar.\n  → We are meeting tomorrow at 5 PM. (Biz ertaga soat 5 da uchrashamiz)\n  → She is flying to London next week. (U keyingi hafta Londonga uchadi)\n\n📌 O'ZGARISH JARAYONI (Changing/developing): Sekin-asta o'zgarib borayotgan holatlar.\n  → The weather is getting colder. (Ob-havo sovib bormoqda)\n  → Your English is improving every day. (Ingliz tilingiz kundan-kunga yaxshilanmoqda)",
    "2️⃣ QANDAY YASALADI?\n\nIjobiy shakl (Affirmative):\n  I + am + verb + ing\n    I am working. (Men ishlayapman)\n    I am eating. (Men yeyapman)\n\n  He/She/It + is + verb + ing\n    She is running. (U yuguryapti)\n    He is sleeping. (U uxlayapti)\n\n  You/We/They + are + verb + ing\n    You are studying. (Siz o'qiyapsiz)\n    They are playing. (Ular o'ynashyapti)\n\n  📌 Verb + -ing qo'shimchasi qoidalari:\n    • Base + -ing: play→playing, eat→eating, sleep→sleeping, read→reading\n    • -e tashlanadi: make→making, come→coming, write→writing, take→taking, dance→dancing\n    • -ie → -y + -ing: lie→lying, die→dying, tie→tying\n    • CVC qoidasi: sit→sitting, run→running, stop→stopping, swim→swimming, get→getting\n    • -l bilan tugasa (British English): travel→travelling, cancel→cancelling",
    "3️⃣ INKOR SHAKLI (Negative)\n\n  I + am not + verb+ing\n  He/She/It + isn't + verb+ing\n  You/We/They + aren't + verb+ing\n\n  🔴 MUHIM: 'am not' qisqartirilmaydi! 'amn't' degan shakl YO'Q.\n  ❌ I isn't working ❌\n  ✅ I am not working ✓\n  ❌ She aren't sleeping ❌\n  ✅ She isn't sleeping ✓\n\n  Misollar:\n    I am not listening to music. (Men musiqa eshitmayapman)\n    He isn't playing football today. (U bugun futbol o'ynamayapti)\n    They aren't coming to the party. (Ular ziyofatga kelishmayapti)\n    She isn't wearing a jacket. (U ko'ylagi kiymagan)",
    "4️⃣ SAVOL SHAKLI (Questions)\n\n  Am + I + verb+ing?\n  Is + he/she/it + verb+ing?\n  Are + you/we/they + verb+ing?\n\n  🔴 MUHIM: Savolda am/is/are sub'ektdan OLDIN keladi!\n  ❌ You are working? ❌ (bu savol emas, balandroq ohangda savol bo'lishi mumkin)\n  ✅ Are you working? ✓ (to'g'ri savol shakli)\n\n  Qisqa javoblar (Short answers):\n    Are you sleeping? → Yes, I am. / No, I'm not.\n    Is he working? → Yes, he is. / No, he isn't.\n    Are they coming? → Yes, they are. / No, they aren't.\n\n  WH-savollar (What/Where/When/Why/How):\n    What are you doing? (Nima qilyapsan?)\n    Where is she going? (U qayerga ketyapti?)\n    Why are they crying? (Nega ular yig'layapti?)\n    How are you feeling? (O'zingizni qanday his qilyapsiz?)",
    "5️⃣ VAQT BELGILARI (Time expressions)\n\n  Present Continuous bilan ishlatiladigan eng muhim vaqt belgilari:\n\n  now (hozir) → I am working now.\n  right now / at the moment (aynan hozir) → She is sleeping right now.\n  currently (hozirda, ayni paytda) → He is currently working on a project.\n  today / tonight (bugun / bugun kechqurun) → We are having dinner tonight.\n  this week/month/year (bu hafta/oy/yil) → I am studying English this month.\n  these days (shu kunlarda) → She is working hard these days.\n  still (hali ham) → He is still sleeping. It's 10 AM!\n  Look! / Listen! (Qarang! / Eshiting!) → Look! It is raining! / Listen! Someone is singing!\n\n  🔥 Present Simple bilan farq:\n    I drink coffee every day. (Simple Present → odat)\n    I am drinking coffee now. (Present Continuous → hozir)\n    ❌ I am drinking coffee every day ❌ (odat uchun NOTO'G'RI)\n    ✅ I drink coffee every day ✓",
    "6️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA FARQLAR (Uzbek vs English)\n\n  O'zbek tilida bir xil fe'l shakli tarjima qilinishi mumkin:\n    'Men ishlayman' → I work (Simple Present) yoki I am working (Present Continuous)\n\n  O'zbeklarning eng keng tarqalgan xatolari:\n    • I working now ❌ → I am working now ✓ (am/is/are unutiladi!)\n    • He is play football ❌ → He is playing football ✓ (-ing qo'shimchasi kerak)\n    • She are reading ❌ → She is reading ✓ (is/are chalkashadi)\n    • We is going ❌ → We are going ✓ (We bilan 'are' ishlatiladi)\n    • I am knowing the answer ❌ → I know the answer ✓ (state verb)\n\n  📌 ESLATMA: 'hozir' so'zi kelsa → Present Continuous kerak deb o'ylamang!\n    I see a bird now. (Men hozir qushni ko'ryapman — see = state verb)\n    I understand the lesson now. (Men hozir darsni tushunyapman — understand = state verb)",
    "7️⃣ STATE VERBS — Present Continuous ishlatilmaydigan fe'llar\n\n  Ayrim fe'llar Present Continuous da ishlatilmaydi. Ular doim Simple Present da keladi, hatto 'hozir' ma'nosida bo'lsa ham:\n\n  🧠 AQLIY FE'LLAR: know, understand, believe, think (fikr), remember, forget, mean\n    I know the answer. (Men javobni bilaman)\n    ❌ I am knowing ❌\n\n  ❤️ HISSIY FE'LLAR: like, love, hate, want, need, prefer, care\n    She likes ice cream. (U muzqaymoqni yaxshi ko'radi)\n    ❌ She is liking ❌\n\n  👁 SEZGI FE'LLARI: see, hear, smell, taste, feel, look (ko'rinmoq), seem\n    I see a beautiful view. (Men go'zal manzarani ko'ryapman)\n    ❌ I am seeing ❌ (bu yerda)\n\n  📌 EGALIK FE'LLARI: have (ega bo'lmoq), own, belong, contain, include\n    He has a car. (Uning mashinasi bor)\n    ❌ He is having ❌ (egalik ma'nosida)\n\n  🔥 LEKIN! Ba'zi fe'llar turli ma'nolarda ishlatilishi mumkin:\n    have → I have a car (egalik) vs I am having dinner (harakat)\n    think → I think it's true (fikr) vs I am thinking about you (jarayon)\n    see → I see you (sezgi) vs I am seeing the doctor (uchrashuv)",
    "8️⃣ BU ZAMON BOSHQA ZAMONLARDAN QANDAY FARQLANADI?\n\nPresent Continuous boshqa zamonlardan quyidagicha farqlanadi:\n\n📌 PC vs Simple Present:\n  PC → hozirgi harakat (now, at the moment)\n    → I am reading a book now.\n  SP → odat, haqiqat (every day, always)\n    → I read books every day.\n  ❌ I am reading books every day ✗\n  ✅ I read books every day ✓\n\n📌 PC vs Simple Past:\n  PC → hozirgi harakat\n    → I am cooking dinner now.\n  SP → o'tmishda tugagan\n    → I cooked dinner yesterday.\n  ❌ I am cooking dinner yesterday ✗\n  ✅ I cooked dinner yesterday ✓\n\n📌 PC vs Present Perfect:\n  PC → hozirgi jarayon (vaqtincha)\n    → I am living with my friend this week.\n  PP → tajriba yoki davomiylik\n    → I have lived here for 5 years.\n\n📌 PC vs Future (will/going to):\n  PC → kelajak rejalari\n    → I am meeting him tomorrow.\n  will → bashorat/va'da\n    → I will help you.\n  going to → oldindan reja\n    → I am going to travel next year.\n\n🔥 ESLATMA: 'now', 'at the moment', 'Look!', 'Listen!' kelsa → 100% Present Continuous!",
  ],
