  rules: [
    "1️⃣ QACHON ISHLATILADI?\n\nPresent Perfect — o'tmishda boshlanib, hozirgi vaqt bilan bog'liq bo'lgan harakatlar uchun ishlatiladi. 4 ta asosiy holat:\n\n📌 NATIJA HOZIR MUHIM (Result): O'tmishdagi harakatning natijasi hozir muhim.\n  → I have lost my keys. (Kalitlarimni yo'qotdim → hozir topolmayapman)\n  → She has finished her homework. (U vazifasini tugatdi → hozir bo'sh)\n\n📌 TAJRIBA (Experience): Hayot davomida qilingan yoki qilinmagan narsalar.\n  → I have never been to Japan. (Men hech qachon Yaponiyada bo'lmaganman)\n  → Have you ever eaten sushi? (Siz hech qachon sushi yegansizmi?)\n\n📌 DAVOMIY HARAKAT (Duration): O'tmishda boshlanib, hozirgacha davom etayotgan harakatlar.\n  → I have lived here for 10 years. (Men bu yerda 10 yil yashayman → hali ham yashayapman)\n  → She has worked here since 2020. (U 2020-dan beri shu yerda ishlaydi)\n\n📌 YAQIN O'TMISH (Just completed): Hozirgina tugagan harakatlar.\n  → He has just left. (U hozirgina ketdi)\n  → We have just arrived. (Biz hozirgina keldik)",
    "2️⃣ QANDAY YASALADI?\n\nIjobiy: have/has + Past Participle (V3)\n  I have played football. (Men futbol o'ynaganman)\n  She has written a letter. (U xat yozdi)\n\n  Regular fe'llar: V3 = V + ed\n    play → played, work → worked, finish → finished\n\n  Irregular fe'llar: V3 ni yod olish kerak (eng muhimlari):\n    go → went → gone (borgan)\n    eat → ate → eaten (yegan)\n    see → saw → seen (ko'rgan)\n    write → wrote → written (yozgan)\n    take → took → taken (olgan)\n    buy → bought → bought (sotib olgan)\n    have → had → had (ega bo'lgan)\n    be → was/were → been (bo'lgan)",
    "3️⃣ YET / ALREADY / JUST — vaqt belgilari\n\n  📌 JUST = HOZIRGINA (yaqin o'tmish)\n    I have just finished my work. (hozirgina tugatdim)\n    She has just left the office. (hozirgina ketdi)\n    → Gapning o'rtasida, have/has dan keyin, V3 dan oldin\n\n  📌 ALREADY = ALLAQACHON (kutilganidan tez)\n    He has already arrived. (U allaqachon yetib keldi)\n    They have already eaten. (Ular allaqachon ovqatlanishdi)\n    → Gapning o'rtasida, have/has dan keyin, V3 dan oldin\n    → Savolda: Have you already finished?\n\n  📌 YET = HALI (inkorda va savollarda)\n    She hasn't arrived yet. (U hali kelmadi)\n    Have you finished yet? (Siz tugatdingizmi?)\n    → Gapning OXIRIDA!",
    "4️⃣ EVER / NEVER — tajriba haqida\n\n  📌 EVER = HECH QACHON (savollarda)\n    Have you ever been to London? (Siz hech qachon Londonda bo'lganmisiz?)\n    Has she ever tried sushi? (U hech qachon sushi yeganmi?)\n\n  📌 NEVER = HECH QACHON (inkor ma'nosida, lekin NOT bilan ishlatilmaydi)\n    I have never seen snow. (Men hech qachon qor ko'rmaganman)\n    ❌ I haven't never seen ❌ (double negative)\n    ✅ I have never seen ✓\n\n  📌 Superlative + Present Perfect:\n    This is the best movie I have ever seen. (Bu men ko'rgan eng yaxshi film)\n    She is the kindest person I have ever met.",
    "5️⃣ FOR / SINCE — qancha vaqt?\n\n  📌 FOR + VAQT MUDDATI (duration)\n    for 10 years, for 2 hours, for a long time\n    I have lived here for 10 years. (10 yildan beri)\n    We have known each other for 5 years.\n\n  📌 SINCE + ANIQ VAQT (starting point)\n    since 2020, since Monday, since I was a child\n    I have lived here since 2020. (2020-dan beri)\n    She has worked here since January.\n\n  🔥 MUHIM FARQ:\n    for + vaqt uzunligi (for 3 hours)\n    since + boshlanish nuqtasi (since 3 o'clock)\n    ❌ I have lived here since 10 years ❌\n    ✅ I have lived here for 10 years ✓",
    "6️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA FARQLAR (Uzbek vs English)\n\n  O'zbek tilida Present Perfect va Simple Past farqi aniq emas:\n    'Men kitob o'qidim' → I read a book (Simple Past) yoki I have read a book (Present Perfect)\n\n  QACHON SIMPLE PAST ISHLATILADI?\n    → Time past: yesterday, last week, 2 years ago, in 2020 (aniq o'tmish vaqti)\n    ❌ I have seen him yesterday ❌\n    ✅ I saw him yesterday ✓\n\n  QACHON PRESENT PERFECT ISHLATILADI?\n    → No time / unfinished / result / experience\n    ✅ I have seen him (when? aniq emas, natija muhim)\n    ✅ I have never seen snow (tajriba)\n    ✅ I have lived here since 2018 (davom etadi)\n\n  O'zbeklarning eng keng tarqalgan xatolari:\n    • I have visited my grandmother yesterday ❌ (yesterday → Simple Past)\n    • I have been to Tashkent last week ❌ (last week → Simple Past)\n    • She has went ❌ → She has gone ✓ (went V2, gone V3)",
    "7️⃣ STATE VERBS — Present Perfect bilan\n\n  State verb'lar Present Perfect da qisqa/aniqlik ma'nosida ishlatiladi:\n    • I have known him for 10 years. (bilish → davomiy holat)\n    • She has always wanted to travel. (xohlash → tajriba)\n    • We have had this car since 2019. (egalik → davom etadi)\n\n  🔥 MUHIM: 'How long' savoli bilan Present Perfect ishlatiladi:\n    How long have you known her? (Qancha vaqtdan beri bilasiz?)\n    How long have you had this job? (Bu ishda qancha vaqtdan beri ishlaysiz?)",
    "8️⃣ BU ZAMON BOSHQA ZAMONLARDAN QANDAY FARQLANADI?\n\nPresent Perfect boshqa zamonlardan quyidagicha farqlanadi:\n\n📌 PP vs Simple Past:\n  PP → tajriba, natija, davomiylik (vaqt aniq emas)\n    → I have visited Paris. (Parijda bo'lganman → tajriba)\n  SP → aniq o'tmish vaqti\n    → I visited Paris last year. (O'tgan yili Parijda bo'ldim)\n\n📌 PP vs Past Continuous:\n  PP → tugallangan harakat, natija\n    → I have read the book. (Kitobni o'qib chiqdim)\n  PC → o'tmishda davom\n    → I was reading the book. (Kitobni o'qiyotgan edim)\n\n📌 PP vs Present Continuous:\n  PP → tajriba, natija\n    → I have eaten lunch. (Tushlikni yeganman)\n  PC → hozirgi harakat\n    → I am eating lunch. (Tushlikni yeyapman)\n\n📌 PP vs Future:\n  PP → o'tmish tajribasi\n    → I have been to London. (Londonda bo'lganman)\n  Future → kelajak\n    → I will go to London. (Londonga boraman)\n\n🔥 ESLATMA: 'ever', 'never', 'just', 'already', 'yet', 'for', 'since' kelsa → Present Perfect!",
  ],
