  rules: [
    "1️⃣ QACHON ISHLATILADI?\n\nPresent Perfect Continuous (PPC) — o'tmishda boshlanib, hozirgacha davom etgan yoki hozir tugagan harakatlar uchun. 4 ta asosiy holat:\n\n📌 DAVOMIYLIK (Duration focus): Harakatning qancha vaqt davom etgani muhim.\n  → I have been studying for 3 hours. (Men 3 soatdan beri o'qiyapman)\n  → She has been working since 8 AM. (U ertalab soat 8 dan beri ishlayapti)\n\n📌 NATIJA HOZIR KO'RINADI (Visible result): Hozir ko'rinadigan natija bor.\n  → My hands are dirty because I have been fixing the car. (Qo'llarim kir, chunki mashina tuzatayotgan edim)\n  → She is tired because she has been running. (U charchagan, chunki yugurayotgan edi)\n\n📌 YAQIN O'TMISH (Recently/Lately): Yaqinda boshlanib davom etayotgan harakatlar.\n  → I have been feeling tired lately. (So'nggi paytlarda charchoq sezyapman)\n  → It has been raining a lot recently. (Yaqinda ko'p yomg'ir yog'di)\n\n📌 VAQTINCHALIK (Temporary): Vaqtinchalik holat yoki yangi odat.\n  → I have been living with my friend while my house is being renovated. (Uyim ta'mirlanayotgani uchun do'stimniki bilan turibman)",
    "2️⃣ QANDAY YASALADI?\n\nIjobiy shakl (Affirmative):\n  have/has + been + verb + -ing\n\n  I / You / We / They → have + been + V-ing\n    I have been working, You have been waiting, We have been studying\n  He / She / It → has + been + V-ing\n    He has been sleeping, She has been reading, It has been raining\n\n  📌 MUHIM: PPC da DOIM 'been' + 'V-ing' birga keladi!\n    have + been + V-ing (uch qismli fe'l)\n\n  📌 -ing qo'shimchasi (PC bilan bir xil qoidalar):\n    • run → running (double n)\n    • write → writing (drop -e)\n    • lie → lying (-ie → -y + ing)",
    "3️⃣ INKOR SHAKLI (Negative)\n\n  I / You / We / They + haven't + been + V-ing\n  He / She / It + hasn't + been + V-ing\n\n  🔴 MUHIM: haven't = have not, hasn't = has not\n  ❌ I haven't been sleeping well lately. (So'nggi paytlarda yaxshi uxlamayapman)\n  ✅ She hasn't been feeling well since Monday. (Dushanbadan beri o'zini yaxshi his qilmayapti)\n  ❌ They haven't been waiting long. (Ular uzoq kutishmadi)\n\n  To'liq shakl: have not / has not + been + V-ing\n    I have not been studying enough. (Yetarlicha o'qimayapman)\n    He has not been working recently. (U yaqinda ishlamayapti)",
    "4️⃣ SAVOL SHAKLI (Questions)\n\n  Have + I/you/we/they + been + V-ing?\n  Has + he/she/it + been + V-ing?\n\n  🔴 MUHIM: have/has sub'ektdan OLDIN keladi, been va V-ing o'zgarmaydi!\n  ✅ Have you been waiting long? ✓\n  ❌ You have been waiting? ✗ (bu savol emas)\n\n  Qisqa javoblar:\n    Have you been studying? → Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.\n    Has she been working? → Yes, she has. / No, she hasn't.\n\n  WH-savollar:\n    How long have you been learning English? (Qancha vaqtdan beri ingliz tili o'rganyapsiz?)\n    What have you been doing all day? (Kun bo'yi nima qilyapsiz?)\n    Where has he been living since 2020? (2020-dan beri qayerda yashayapti?)",
    "5️⃣ VAQT BELGILARI (Time expressions)\n\n  PPC bilan ishlatiladigan asosiy vaqt belgilari:\n\n  ⏳ FOR + vaqt muddati (qancha vaqt?)\n    for 2 hours, for 3 years, for a long time, for ages\n    → I have been waiting for 30 minutes.\n\n  📅 SINCE + boshlanish nuqtasi (qachondan beri?)\n    since 2020, since Monday, since 5 o'clock, since morning\n    → She has been working since 9 AM.\n\n  🌅 ALL DAY / ALL MORNING / ALL WEEK\n    → It has been raining all day.\n\n  📆 LATELY / RECENTLY (so'nggi paytlarda)\n    → I have been feeling tired lately.\n\n  ❓ HOW LONG (qancha vaqt? — eng keng tarqalgan savol)\n    How long have you been studying English?",
    "6️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA FARQLAR (Uzbek vs English)\n\n  O'zbek tilida Present Perfect va Present Perfect Continuous farqi aniq emas:\n    'Men 3 soat o'qidim' → I have studied (PP) yoki I have been studying (PPC)\n\n  PRESENT PERFECT (PP) → NATIJA muhim:\n    I have written 3 emails. (3 ta xat yozdim → natija: xatlar tayyor)\n    She has read the book. (Kitobni o'qib chiqdi → natija: kitob tugadi)\n\n  PRESENT PERFECT CONTINUOUS (PPC) → DAVOMIYLIK muhim:\n    I have been writing emails all morning. (Tongdan beri xat yozyapman → davomiylik)\n    She has been reading that book for a week. (Bir haftadan beri o'qiyapti → hali tugamagan)\n\n  O'zbeklarning eng keng tarqalgan xatolari:\n    • I have been knowing him ❌ → I have known him ✓ (know = state verb)\n    • She has been having a car ❌ → She has had a car ✓ (have = state verb)\n    • How long do you learn English? ❌ → How long have you been learning English? ✓\n    • I have been working here since 2 years ❌ → I have been working here for 2 years ✓",
    "7️⃣ PRESENT PERFECT vs PRESENT PERFECT CONTINUOUS — batafsil farq!\n\n  🔥 PP = NATIJA (completed action, result visible)\n    I have painted the room. (Natija: xona bo'yalgan, ish tugagan)\n    She has written three books. (Natija: uchta kitob yozilgan)\n    How many pages have you read? (Necha sahifa o'qidingiz?)\n\n  🔥 PPC = DAVOMIYLIK (action in progress, duration emphasized)\n    I have been painting the room all day. (Kun bo'yi xonani bo'yayapman → hali tugamagan)\n    She has been writing a novel. (Roman yozayapti → hali tugamagan)\n    How long have you been reading? (Qancha vaqtdan beri o'qiyapsiz?)\n\n  📌 SODDA QOIDA:\n    PP → 'How many / How much' (miqdor va natija)\n    PPC → 'How long' (davomiylik va jarayon)\n\n  📌 State verb'lar PPC da ishlatilmaydi:\n    ❌ I have been knowing → ✅ I have known\n    ❌ I have been wanting → ✅ I have wanted\n    ❌ I have been belonging → ✅ I have belonged",
  ],
