  rules: [
    "1️⃣ QACHON ISHLATILADI?\n\nFuture Perfect to'rtta asosiy holatda ishlatiladi:\n\n📌 TUGALLANGAN HARAKAT (completed by + time): Kelajakda biror vaqtga qadar biror ishni tugatgan bo'lamiz.\n  → By 6 PM, I will have finished my work. (Soat 6 ga qadar ishimni tugatgan bo'laman)\n  → She will have graduated by next year. (U keyingi yilga qadar o'qishni tugatgan bo'ladi)\n\n📌 NATIJA MUHIM (result at future point): Kelajakdagi nuqtada biror ishning natijasi mavjud bo'ladi.\n  → Don't call at 7 — I will have left the office. (Soat 7 da qo'ng'iroq qilmang — men ketgan bo'laman)\n  → By the time you arrive, we will have had dinner. (Siz kelguningizcha, biz ovqat yegan bo'lamiz)\n\n📌 DAVOMIYLIK (duration by then): Kelajakda biror vaqtgacha qancha vaqt davom etganligini ko'rsatadi.\n  → Next month, I will have lived here for 5 years. (Keyingi oy, men bu yerda 5 yil yashagan bo'laman)\n  → By 2026, they will have been married for 10 years. (2026 yilga qadar ular 10 yil turmush qurgan bo'ladilar)\n\n📌 TAXMIN (assumption about now): Hozirgi vaqtda biror ish allaqachon bajarilgan bo'lishi mumkin.\n  → Don't worry — he will have already arrived by now. (Xavotir olmang — u allaqachon yetib kelgan bo'ladi)\n  → She will have heard the news by now. (U yangilikni eshitgan bo'ladi)",
    "2️⃣ QANDAY YASALADI?\n\nSubject + will have + Past Participle (V3)\n\n  I will have finished → Men tugatgan bo'laman\n  She will have left → U ketgan bo'ladi\n  They will have arrived → Ular yetib kelgan bo'ladilar\n\n  Regular fe'llar: V3 = V + ed\n    finish → finished, work → worked, clean → cleaned\n\n  Irregular fe'llar (eng muhimlari):\n    eat → eaten (I will have eaten)\n    write → written (She will have written)\n    see → seen (They will have seen)\n    go → gone (He will have gone)\n    be → been (We will have been)\n    do → done (I will have done)\n    make → made (She will have made)\n    build → built (They will have built)\n    leave → left (He will have left)\n    buy → bought (She will have bought)",
    "3️⃣ INKOR SHAKLI (Negative)\n\n  Subject + won't have / will not have + V3\n\n  I won't have finished by 6. (Men soat 6 ga qadar tugatmagan bo'laman)\n  She won't have arrived before dinner. (U kechki ovqatdan oldin kelmagan bo'ladi)\n  They won't have completed the project by Friday. (Ular juma kuniga qadar loyihani tugatmagan bo'ladilar)\n\n  🔴 MUHIM: won't have dan keyin V3 (past participle) ishlatiladi!\n  ❌ I won't have finish ❌\n  ✅ I won't have finished ✓\n\n  ❌ She won't has arrived ❌\n  ✅ She won't have arrived ✓",
    "4️⃣ SAVOL SHAKLI (Questions)\n\n  Will + subject + have + V3?\n\n  Will you have finished by 6? (Soat 6 ga qadar tugatgan bo'lasizmi?)\n  Will she have arrived before the meeting? (U yig'ilishdan oldin kelgan bo'ladimi?)\n  Will they have completed the project by Friday? (Ular juma kuniga qadar loyihani tugatgan bo'ladilarmi?)\n\n  Qisqa javoblar (Short answers):\n    Will you have finished? → Yes, I will have. / No, I won't have.\n\n  WH-savollar:\n    What will you have done by then? (U vaqtga qadar nima qilgan bo'lasiz?)\n    How many reports will she have written by Friday? (U juma kuniga qadar qancha hisobot yozgan bo'ladi?)\n    Where will they have gone by that time? (Ular o'sha vaqtga qadar qayerga ketgan bo'ladilar?)",
    "5️⃣ VAQT BELGILARI (Time Markers)\n\n  📌 by + vaqt: by 5 PM, by Friday, by next week, by 2030, by tomorrow\n    I will have finished by tomorrow. (Men ertagacha tugatgan bo'laman)\n\n  📌 before + vaqt: before you arrive, before dinner, before midnight\n    She will have left before midnight. (U yarim tundan oldin ketgan bo'ladi)\n\n  📌 by the time + gap: by the time you get here, by the time I retire, by the time we arrive\n    By the time you arrive, we will have had dinner. (Siz kelguningizcha, biz ovqat yegan bo'lamiz)\n\n  📌 already, just, yet (savol/inkorda):\n    I will have already finished by then. (Men u vaqtga qadar allaqachon tugatgan bo'laman)\n    Will you have finished your homework yet? (Siz uy vazifasini tugatgan bo'lasizmi?)",
    "6️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA FARQLAR (Uzbek vs English)\n\n  O'zbek tilida 'tugatgan bo'laman' o'rniga ko'pincha 'tugataman' deyiladi, ammo ingliz tilida bu ikki zamon FARQLI:\n\n  Future Simple: I will finish at 5. (Soat 5 da tugataman → kelajakda qilaman)\n  Future Perfect: I will have finished by 5. (Soat 5 ga qadar tugatgan bo'laman → 5 dan OLDIN tugagan)\n\n  O'zbeklarning eng keng tarqalgan xatolari:\n    • By next week I will finish the project ❌ (by = FP kerak)\n      → I will have finished the project by next week ✓\n    • I will have finish my homework ❌ (V3 emas)\n      → I will have finished my homework ✓\n    • She will have been finished ❌ (been ortiqcha)\n      → She will have finished ✓\n    • Will you have been done? ❌ (been ortiqcha)\n      → Will you have done? ✓",
    "7️⃣ FUTURE PERFECT vs FUTURE CONTINUOUS vs FUTURE PERFECT CONTINUOUS\n\n  Uch zamonni solishtirish orqali farqni tushunamiz:\n\n  🔷 Future Perfect (FP) — by + vaqt → TUGAGAN (result/completed by future point)\n    By 5 PM, I will have finished work.\n    (Soat 5 ga qadar ishni tugatgan bo'laman → ish TUGAGAN)\n\n  🔷 Future Continuous (FC) — at + vaqt → DAVOM (in progress at future point)\n    At 5 PM, I will be working.\n    (Soat 5 da ishlayotgan bo'laman → ish DAVOM etmoqda)\n\n  🔷 Future Perfect Continuous (FPC) — by + vaqt + for + duration → MUDDAT + DAVOM\n    By 5 PM, I will have been working for 8 hours.\n    (Soat 5 ga qadar 8 soat ishlab bo'laman → muddat davom etgan)\n\n  📌 by + TIME qoidasi: by = 'ga qadar' yoki 'dan oldin'. FP bilan by har doim 'tugallanganlik'ni ta'kidlaydi.\n    'By Friday' = juma kelguniga qadar tugagan bo'ladi.\n    → By Friday, I will have sent the report. (Juma kelguniga qadar hisobotni jo'natgan bo'laman)",
  ],
