  rules: [
    "1️⃣ QACHON ISHLATILADI?\n\nFuture Perfect Continuous uchta asosiy holatda ishlatiladi:\n\n📌 DAVOMIYLIK (duration up to a future point): Kelajakda biror vaqtgacha biror ishni qancha vaqt davomida bajarayotgan bo'lamiz.\n  → By 5 PM, I will have been working for 8 hours. (Soat 5 ga qadar men 8 soat ishlab bo'laman)\n  → Next year, she will have been teaching for 20 years. (Kelasi yil u 20 yil dars bergan bo'ladi)\n\n📌 SABAB-NATIJA (cause-effect before future): Kelajakdagi biror narsaning sababi — oldin davom etgan harakat.\n  → He will be tired because he will have been working all day. (U charchagan bo'ladi, chunki kun bo'yi ishlagan bo'ladi)\n  → Her English will be excellent because she will have been studying for years. (Uning ingliz tili zo'r bo'ladi, chunki yillar davomida o'rgangan bo'ladi)\n\n📌 NATIJA KO'RINADI (visible result): Kelajakdagi biror nuqtada biror uzoq davom etgan harakatning natijasi ko'rinadi.\n  → When you arrive, you will see that I will have been painting the room. (Kelganingizda ko'rasiz, men xonani bo'yagan bo'laman)\n  → By the time we meet, I will have been preparing for the presentation. (Uchrashgunimizcha, men taqdimotga tayyorlanib bo'laman)",
    "2️⃣ QANDAY YASALADI?\n\nSubject + will have been + verb + ing\n\n  I will have been working → Men ishlab bo'laman (8 soat)\n  She will have been studying → U o'qib bo'ladi (3 yil)\n  They will have been waiting → Ular kutib bo'ladilar (2 soat)\n\n  📌 FE'LGA -ing QO'SHISH QOIDALARI:\n    • Aksariyat fe'llar: verb + ing → work → working, study → studying\n    • -e bilan tugagan fe'llar: e tushadi + ing → write → writing, take → taking\n    • CVC (undosh-unli-undosh): oxirgi harf takrorlanadi → run → running, sit → sitting\n    • -ie bilan tugagan fe'llar: ie → y + ing → lie → lying, die → dying\n\n  🔥 MUHIM: will have been + V-ing (V3 emas! Future Perfect dan farqli!)",
    "3️⃣ INKOR SHAKLI (Negative)\n\n  Subject + won't have been + V-ing\n\n  I won't have been waiting long. (Men uzoq kutgan bo'lmayman)\n  She won't have been studying English for 10 years by 2026. (U 2026 ga qadar 10 yil ingliz tili o'qigan bo'lmaydi)\n  They won't have been living here for very long. (Ular bu yerda juda uzoq yashagan bo'lmaydilar)\n\n  🔴 MUHIM:\n  ❌ I won't have been worked ❌ (worked emas!)\n  ✅ I won't have been working ✓ (working to'g'ri)\n\n  ❌ She won't has been waiting ❌\n  ✅ She won't have been waiting ✓",
    "4️⃣ SAVOL SHAKLI (Questions)\n\n  Will + subject + have been + V-ing?\n\n  Will you have been working for 8 hours by 6 PM? (Soat 6 ga qadar 8 soat ishlagan bo'lasizmi?)\n  Will she have been teaching for 20 years next year? (U kelasi yil 20 yil dars bergan bo'ladimi?)\n  Will they have been living here for 5 years by then? (Ular o'sha vaqtga qadar bu yerda 5 yil yashagan bo'ladilarmi?)\n\n  Qisqa javoblar:\n    Will you have been studying? → Yes, I will have. / No, I won't have.\n\n  WH-savollar:\n    How long will you have been working by 5 PM? (Soat 5 ga qadar qancha vaqt ishlagan bo'lasiz?)\n    What will she have been doing all morning? (U ertalab bo'yi nima qilgan bo'ladi?)",
    "5️⃣ VAQT BELGILARI (Time Markers)\n\n  📌 by + vaqt: by 5 PM, by Friday, by next year, by 2030\n    I will have been working here for 5 years by next month. (Kelasi oygacha bu yerda 5 yil ishlagan bo'laman)\n\n  📌 for + muddat: for 3 hours, for 10 years, for a long time\n    She will have been studying for 3 hours by the time we arrive.\n\n  📌 since + boshlanish: since 2020, since morning, since I was a child\n    By 2026, he will have been working here since 2016. (10 yil)\n\n  📌 by the time + gap:\n    By the time you get here, I will have been waiting for an hour.\n\n  📌 all day/morning/night:\n    He will have been working all day.",
    "6️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA FARQLAR (Uzbek vs English)\n\n  O'zbek tilida Future Perfect Continuous ning aniq ekvivalenti YO'Q. O'zbeklar ko'pincha 'tugatgan bo'laman' (FP) va 'ishlab bo'laman' (FPC) ni aralashtiradilar.\n\n  Future Perfect: I will have finished work by 5. → Ishni soat 5 ga qadar TUGATGAN bo'laman (result)\n  Future Perfect Continuous: I will have been working for 8 hours by 5. → Soat 5 ga qadar 8 soat ISHLAB bo'laman (duration)\n\n  O'zbeklarning eng keng tarqalgan xatolari:\n    • I will have been work here for 10 years ❌ (work emas, working!)\n      → I will have been working here for 10 years ✓\n    • I will have been studied for 3 hours ❌ (studied V3 emas!)\n      → I will have been studying for 3 hours ✓\n    • By next year, she will have been teaching (duration: to'g'ri)\n    • By next year, she will have taught 100 students (result: to'g'ri)\n    • I will have been being a teacher ❌ (be stative verb, ing olmaydi)\n      → I will have been a teacher for 10 years (buni FP bilan aytamiz)",
    "7️⃣ STATIVE VERB CHEKLAMALARI + FPC vs FP vs FC\n\n  🔴 STATIVE VERBS: FPC bilan ishlatib bo'lmaydi! State verb'lar 'ing' qabul qilmaydi.\n\n  State verb → Future Perfect (FP) ishlatiladi, FPC EMAS:\n    know: By 2026, I will have known her for 10 years ✓\n    ❌ I will have been knowing her for 10 years ❌\n    have (egalik): By next year, I will have had this car for 5 years ✓\n    ❌ I will have been having this car ❌\n    be: By then, I will have been a doctor for 10 years ✓\n    ❌ I will have been being a doctor ❌\n\n  🔷 UCH ZAMON SOLISHTIRMASI:\n\n  Future Simple (will + V1) — KELAJAKDA QILAMAN\n    → At 6 PM, I will work. (Soat 6 da ishlayman)\n\n  Future Continuous (will be + V-ing) — KELAJAKDA DAVOM\n    → At 6 PM, I will be working. (Soat 6 da ishlayotgan bo'laman)\n\n  Future Perfect (will have + V3) — KELAJAKDA TUGATGAN\n    → By 6 PM, I will have finished work. (Soat 6 ga qadar ishni tugatgan bo'laman)\n\n  Future Perfect Continuous (will have been + V-ing) — KELAJAKDA MA'LUM MUDDAT DAVOM ETGAN\n    → By 6 PM, I will have been working for 8 hours. (Soat 6 ga qadar 8 soat ishlab bo'laman)\n\n  📌 FPC = DURATION UP TO A POINT (qancha vaqt davom etganini ko'rsatadi)\n  📌 FP = COMPLETED BY A POINT (tugallanganlikni ko'rsatadi)",
  ],
